  "displayName": "sgm-006 default band (equipment-scoped catch-all)",
  "description": "FIX 5 (2026-07-31) — sgm-006 (Arburg Allrounder 470A, v4-SGM-012) had NO recipe of its own, so recipe:hotrunner_temp_band / hotrunner_control_limits stayed dormant or fell onto a band authored for a different machine — and its actual process then sat exactly ON an alarm line (measured hotrunnerTempC mean 225.00 degC = the warn-lower it was being judged against). A real machine does not hold its setpoint on its own alarm threshold. This recipe re-centres the bands on THIS machine's real setpoint: nozzle SOLL 225 degC (machines-sgm/src/config.ts:385 nozzleSetpointC=225, barrel [195,205,215,220]) so 225 sits in the MIDDLE of its band, not on the edge. Widths mirror the sgm-004 default. mouldTempC band [80,90] is the PA-resin norm (mould TCU target 87.5 degC, MOULD_TCU_TARGET_C). Only the two signals we can calibrate from the machine spec are bound here; pressures/cushion/partMass stay dormant (no per-machine drawing/process sheet yet) so no un-calibrated band can raise a false alarm.",
  "match": {
    "equipment": "sgm-006"
  },
